  <data name="SharePolicy" xml:space="preserve"><value>Prepare {0} photo(s) as JPEG copies: at most 1600 pixels on the longest side, never enlarged, at 85% quality. Batches are limited to 20 photos and 20 MiB; your mail provider may have a lower limit. Only the first frame is used. Common embedded descriptive metadata is retained; GPS, face regions and sidecars are not copied. Originals and selection remain unchanged.&#x0a;&#x0a;Windows Share passes the copies to an app you choose. Email opens your default mail app and the copies folder: you must attach the JPEG files yourself, because mailto links cannot reliably attach files.&#x0a;&#x0a;Temporary copies are kept locally for 7 days, then removed on the next app launch or share. Save a separate copy for long-lived drafts.</value></data>
